{
 "fix": "hwskin_item_rest",
 "archive": "ITEM.VDK",
 "stock_archive_md5": "c82ccc877218e2586400ce6c1a151925",
 "client_build": "b303 2022-02-11 (PRISTINE)",
 "purpose": "Remaining software-skinned meshes in ITEM.VDK, converted to hardware skinning. Software-skinned meshes ship without a BONE_PALETTE; any client path that assigns a GPU-skinning material on the mere presence of a NiSkinningMeshModifier then draws them with whatever bone matrices the previous draw left in the constant registers. Converting them removes that class of defect and puts the deform on the GPU.",
 "change": "NiSkinningMeshModifier USE_SOFTWARE_SKINNING (Flags&1) cleared (0x0003 -> 0x0002); sync points 2 -> 1 ([0x8020,0x8030]/[0x8040,0x8030] -> [0x8020]/[0x8040]); CPU deform-output POSITION/NORMAL streams dropped and replaced by ONE interleaved GPU-readable vertex stream at usage/access (1,18) -- [TEXCOORD, POSITION_BP, NORMAL_BP, BLENDINDICES, BLENDWEIGHT] stride 48, or [COLOR, TEXCOORD, POSITION_BP, NORMAL_BP, BLENDINDICES, BLENDWEIGHT] stride 52 where the mesh carries an authored COLOR channel -- plus a BONE_PALETTE stream at usage/access (3,3); material DefaultRag2ShaderNoSkin -> DefaultRag2ShaderSkin and DefaultRag2ShaderNoSkin_Spec -> DefaultRag2ShaderSkinSpecular; block count, block order and every Ptr/Ref held constant (freed NiDataStream slots rewritten as unreferenced 0-byte stubs, not deleted); all edits by splicing.",
